<objective>
Implement control grouping into named programs so organizations can track compliance across logical security domains (e.g., "Access Control Program", "Encryption Program") instead of framework-flat control lists — closing the gap versus Probo and OpenLane Core.

**Program document schema:**
```json
{
  "id": "prog-{uuid}",
  "tenantId": "...",
  "name": "Access Control Program",
  "description": "...",
  "framework_id": "soc2",
  "owner": "...",
  "control_ids": ["ctrl-001", "ctrl-002"],
  "created_at": "...",
  "updated_at": "..."
}
```

**Status rollup logic:**
- For each control_id, look up latest compliance check result in `compliance_results` collection
- Count passing (status=pass), failing (status=fail), not_assessed (no result)
- `compliant`: passing >= 80% of total AND failing == 0
- `at_risk`: any failing > 0
- `in_progress`: else (some passing, rest not_assessed)

